  "final_message": "The bug was in `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py`. After a successful gateway refund it set `payment[\"ok\"] = \"refunded\"` instead of `payment[\"status\"] = \"refunded\"`. The payment status therefore stayed `succeeded`. I changed line 53 to use `\"status\"`.\n\nThe full suite now passes (25 tests) and mypy is clean. mypy had also flagged the bad key (`TypedDict \"Payment\" has no key \"ok\"`).\n\nI added your reproduction as `tests/test_refund_full.py` and wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.",
